      "text": "Let's denote the roots of the polynomial equation \\(x^3 - 20x^2 + 18x - 7 = 0\\) by \\(r\\), \\(s\\), and \\(t\\). According to Vieta's formulas, for a polynomial of the form \\(ax^3 + bx^2 + cx + d = 0\\) with roots \\(r\\), \\(s\\), and \\(t\\):\n\n\\[\nr + s + t = -\\frac{b}{a} = 20,\n\\]\n\\[\nrs + rt + st = \\frac{c}{a} = 18,\n\\]\n\\[\nrst = -\\frac{d}{a} = 7.\n\\]\n\nWe need to find the value of \\((1+r)(1+s)(1+t)\\). Expanding the product \\((1+r)(1+s)(1+t)\\), we get:\n\n\\[\n(1+r)(1+s)(1+t) = 1 + r + s + t + rs + rt + st + rst.\n\\]\n\nUsing Vieta's formulas, we know that \\(r + s + t = 20\\) and \\(rst = 7\\). Substituting these values into the expression, we have:\n\n\\[\n(1+r)(1+s)(1+t) = 1 + 20 + rs + rt + st + 7.\n\\]\n\nNext, we need to find the value of \\(rs + rt + st\\). Using the identity for the sum of the products of the roots taken two at a time, we have:\n\n\\[\nrs + rt + st = r(s+t) + t(s+r) = r(-20 - r) + t(-20 - r) = -20(r + t) - r^2 - t^2.\n\\]\n\nSince \\(r + t = 20 - s\\), we can substitute this into the expression:\n\n\\[\nrs + rt + st = -20(20 - s) - r^2 - t^2 = -400 + 20s - r^2 - t^2.\n\\]\n\nWe know from Vieta's formulas that \\(s + t = 20 - r\\) and \\(r^2 + t^2 = (r+t)^2 - 2rt = 400 - 2s(r + t) = 400 - 2s(20 - r) = 400 - 40s + 2rs\\). Therefore:\n\n\\[\nrs + rt + st = -400 + 20s + 400 - 40s + 2rs - r^2 - t^2 = -20s + 2rs.\n\\]\n\nGiven that \\(s + t = 20 - r\\) and \\(rst = 7\\), we need to find the value of \\(r\\), \\(s\\), and \\(t\\). From the polynomial, we know that \\(r\\), \\(s\\), and \\(t\\) are the roots, and by trying integer values that satisfy these equations, we find that \\(r = 7\\), \\(s = 3\\), and \\(t = \\frac{1}{7}\\) or similar permutations that satisfy the polynomial. However, we don't need the exact values of \\(r\\), \\(s\\), and \\(t\\) to find the sum \\(rs + rt + st\\). Instead, we use the identity for the sum of the products of the roots taken two at a time:\n\n\\[\nrs + rt + st = 18.\n\\]\n\nThus:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{rs + rt + st}{2} = 9.\n\\]\n\nSubstituting this back into our expression, we get:\n\n\\[\n(1+r)(1+s)(1+t) = 1 + 20 + 18 + 7 = 46.\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\((1+r)(1+s)(1+t)\\) is \\(\\boxed{46}\\).",
