      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "We begin by using Vieta's formulas, which apply to any polynomial $a_n x^n + a_{n-1} x^{n-1} + \\dots + a_1 x + a_0 = 0$. For a polynomial of the form $x^3 + a_2 x^2 + a_1 x + a_0 = 0$, the relationships we look for are:\n\n1. (Sums of roots taken one at a time): $r + s + t = -a_2$\n2. (Sums of roots taken two at a time): $rs + rt + st = a_1$\n3. (Product of roots): $rst = -a_0$\n\nApplying the given polynomial $x^3 - 20x^2 + 18x - 7 = 0$ to these formulas, we find:\n\n1. The sum of roots: $r + s + t = -(-20) = 20$.\n2. The sum of the products of roots taken two at a time: $rs + rt + st = 18$.\n3. The product of the roots: $rst = -(-7) = 7$.\n\nNext, we set up the expression $(1+r)(1+s)(1+t)$, expand it, and look for a connection to either of the sums from the previous formula.\n\nUpon extraction, we get:\n\\[\n(1+r)(1+s)(1+t) = 1 + (r+s+t) + (rs+rt+st) + rst\n\\]\n\nSubstituting the values we found from Vieta's formulas:\n\\[\n1 + 20 + 18 + 7 = 46\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the result is $(1+r)(1+s)(1+t) = \\boxed{46}$.",
