      "text": "We start by expanding $(1+r)(1+s)(1+t):$\n\\begin{align*}\n(1+r)(1+s)(1+t) &= (1+rs+t+r+s+rt+st+rs+st) \\\\\n&= (1 + (r+s)+rt+st+rt+st) \\\\\n&= (1 + 2(r+s+rt+st)).\n\\end{align*}\nWe know that $r,$ $s,$ and $t$ are roots of the equation $x^3 - 20x^2 + 18x - 7 = 0,$ so we can write it as:\n\\begin{align*}\nx^3 - 20x^2 + 18x - 7 &= 0 \\\\\n(x-r)(x-s)(x-t) &= 0 \\\\\n(x-r)(x-s)(x-t) &= 0.\n\\end{align*}\nExpanding $(x-r)(x-s)(x-t),$ we get:\n\\begin{align*}\n(x-r)(x-s)(x-t) &= x(x)(x) - x(r+s+t) + rs+st + rt \\\\\n&= x^3 - x(r+s+t) + rs+st + rt \\\\\n&= x^3 - x(20) + 18x - 7 \\\\\n&= x^3 - 20x^2 + 18x - 7.\n\\end{align*}\nFinally, we substitute $r,$ $s,$ and $t$ with their respective conjugate roots:\n\\begin{align*}\n(1+r)(1+s)(1+t) &= 1^3 - 20(1) + 18(1) - 7 \\\\\n&= -1.\n\\end{align*}",
